e Aspen Acres Burn Scar.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nBeulah and San Isabel.\n\nThis includes the following high risk locations...\nBeulah Water Intake, Northcreek Road county line to Red Mountain Camp\nand Northcreek Road from Red Mountain Camp to Beulah.","ends":"2026-08-24T20:30:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Custer, CO; Pueblo, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.fa7b485eb04553cc64862a4970c82454b3943aec.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.fa7b485eb04553cc64862a4970c82454b3943aec.001.1"},{"event":"Severe Thunderstorm Warning","headline":"Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued August 24 at 5:22PM MDT until August 24 at 5:45PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"At 521 PM MDT, a severe thunderstorm was located near Hanover, or 22\nmiles north of Pueblo Airport, moving east at 15 mph.\n\nHAZARD...60 mph wind gusts.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Expect damage to roofs, siding, and trees.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nSoutheastern Colorado Springs, Fountain, Hanover, Pinon, Pueblo\nDepot, Pueblo West, and Security-Widefield.","ends":"2026-08-24T17:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"El Paso, CO; Pueblo, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6a59767dd2a482b6fdaf3144e6adacb4202ff227.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6a59767dd2a482b6fdaf3144e6adacb4202ff227.002.1"},{"event":"Flash Flood Watch","headline":"Flash Flood Watch issued August 24 at 1:22PM MDT until August 24 at 9:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flash flooding and debris flows caused by excessive rainfall\nwill be possible over the Aspen Acres Burn Scar.\n\n* WHERE...Aspen Acres Burn Scar.\n\n* WHEN...From Tuesday afternoon through Tuesday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Heavy rainfall over the Aspen Acres Burn Scar is expected\nup to and during the period of the watch. Residents near the Aspen\nAcres Burn Scar should prepare for debris flows and stay up to date\nwith information from local authorities. Heavy rainfall could\ntrigger flash flooding of low-lying areas and debris flows in and\nnear recent wildfire burn scars.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- National Weather Service Meteorologists are forecasting heavy\nrainfall over the burn scar, which may lead to flash flooding and\ndebris flows.\n- Some locations that may experience flash flooding include...\nBeulah, San Isabel and Highways 165 and 78 in and around the\nAspen Acres Burn Scar.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-08-24T21:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Wet Mountains between 6300 and 10000Ft; Wet Mountains above 10000 Ft; Pueblo Vicinity/Pueblo County Below 6300 Feet","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.04b1051eae68182634e426b4d232eead38a5a6c9.001.2","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.04b1051eae68182634e426b4d232eead38a5a6c9.001.2"},{"event":"Flash Flood Watch","headline":"Flash Flood Watch issued August 24 at 1:22PM MDT until August 25 at 8:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flash flooding and debris flows caused by excessive rainfall\nwill be possible over the Aspen Acres Burn Scar.\n\n* WHERE...Aspen Acres Burn Scar.\n\n* WHEN...From Tuesday afternoon through Tuesday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Heavy rainfall over the Aspen Acres Burn Scar is expected\nup to and during the period of the watch. Residents near the Aspen\nAcres Burn Scar should prepare for debris flows and stay up to date\nwith information from local authorities. Heavy rainfall could\ntrigger flash flooding of low-lying areas and debris flows in and\nnear recent wildfire burn scars.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- National Weather Service Meteorologists are forecasting heavy\nrainfall over the burn scar, which may lead to flash flooding and\ndebris flows.\n- Some locations that may experience flash flooding include...\nBeulah, San Isabel and Highways 165 and 78 in and around the\nAspen Acres Burn Scar.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends